uzman khan a 28 year old man from  staffordshire  is the suspect behind yesterday's london  bridge knife attack  he was an islamic terrorist convicted in  2012 and released  on license in 2018 khan was known to the  security services  and believed to be wearing an electronic  tag he was wrestled to the ground by  members of the public  and then shot by specialist firearm  officers  a suicide vest he was wearing is  believed to be a fake  police say two people a man and a woman  were killed in the attack  three people a man and two women were  injured  two of them seriously the prime minister  said the incident showed the need for  tougher sentencing  it is a mistake to allow  serious and violent criminals to come  out of  prison early and it is very important  that we get out of that habit and that  we enforce  the appropriate sentences for dangerous  criminals  especially for terrorists  last night the government faced tough  questions about how a known terrorist  was able to carry out such a brutal  attack  i have just come from cobra and the  meeting chaired by the prime minister  and of course there's various strands of  information that's coming together  but this is a police investigation and  so it's inappropriate for me to  comment on reporting or even elements of  reporting that are speculative  police say the attack began as khan was  attending an event  at fishmongers hall on the north side of  london bridge  cordons remain in place but police say  they're not looking for anyone else in  connection with these tragic events  noel phillips sky news
 

